{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1046256-newbie-questions","id":1046256,"title":"Newbie questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-09T05:36:02-08:00","id":1046256,"title":"Newbie questions","content":"1. A mage casts a spell.Are there outward signs he's done it? (arms moving around, saying arcane words etc)<br /> 2. If so, if cast on the fly, are there visible signs he's done so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T05:45:05-08:00","id":1046264,"title":"","content":"Unless he used Yantras (p.119) it's not visible. But I tend to narrate that as a mage you can notice this kind of &quot;spacing out&quot; and discern if someone is inviting Supernal.<br /> Other thing is Nimbus ( p.88) which flashes when you cast a spell. It's only visible under Mage Sight, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T06:13:41-08:00","id":1046275,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1046256-newbie-questions?p=1046264#post1046264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless he used Yantras (p.119) it's not visible. But I tend to narrate that as a mage you can notice this kind of &quot;spacing out&quot; and discern if someone is inviting Supernal.<br /> Other thing is Nimbus ( p.88) which flashes when you cast a spell. It's only visible under Mage Sight, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. <br /> <br /> Another question. In one of the books it states that the path connected to Arcadia may or may not be the same Arcadia as in Changeling the Lost . I would say they are one and the same. So if that's the case, then what does that mean? What would the Gentry be considered in mage term? <br /> <br /> Also , they pooled their merits together to get a headquarters so to speak. In the basement, behind the wall there is a small cave with a dark opening. I want this to be an all supernatural types charging station so to speak at least for Mages, Sin Eaters and Werewolves. I know that vampires and Changelings are too particular to use it. Would this be too over reaching?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas","name":"Blue Thomas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4135_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T06:27:30-08:00","id":1046281,"title":"","content":"As far as I know the official rulling is that they are not the same. One is kind of &quot;internet&quot; of symbols that are &quot;nowhere&quot; and the other is a place. Sadly, I'm not versed enough in Changeling to say what consequencies it would make if they were the same. I'm waiting for a Changeling 2E to jump into it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Talking about chargin other splats. Nothing stops you from telling your player to buy Dedicated Locus merit or giving it to them for free.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T07:04:48-08:00","id":1046296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Thomas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1046256-newbie-questions?p=1046275#post1046275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would the Gentry be considered in mage term?</div> </div> </div> </div>Imperial Mysteries had a thinly disguised reference to the Gentry as the Old Gods of the Thistle; it's a pretty good explanation for the Gentry if they are Supernal beings. Moinen is correct though that the working assumption as of 2e is that they're different places/entities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Would this be too over reaching? </div> </div> </div>I dont' think it's impossible, but it's pretty unlikely. However it's a pretty small detail so I wouldn't worry too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T07:20:56-08:00","id":1046302,"title":"","content":"1st Edition spent a lot of time and energy teasing the possibility of Mage Arcadia and Changeling Arcadia being the same place, but there was never any payoff. 2e made the call to stop teasing and make them explicitly two different places. Well, one distinct place and one distinct collection of Supernal symbols, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T09:57:18-08:00","id":1046361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blue Thomas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1046256-newbie-questions?p=1046275#post1046275\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you.<br /> Also , they pooled their merits together to get a headquarters so to speak. In the basement, behind the wall there is a small cave with a dark opening. I want this to be an all supernatural types charging station so to speak at least for Mages, Sin Eaters and Werewolves. I know that vampires and Changelings are too particular to use it. Would this be too over reaching?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess you are speaking about places of power like dragon nest's (Ordo Dracul), Loci (werewolf), Hallows (mage), etc...<br /> <br /> Rules as Written, I could say that no, a place gives only one type of &quot;soda&quot;. Cannot choose more than one flavor. If you want a place to have more than one flavor of soda, you can always houserule it, but with common sense. Is what I do.<br /> <br /> For example, in my games I play with the concept of Resonance, and allow all kind of supernaturals benefit of some places of power if the resonance of the place is adecuate for that supernatural.<br /> <br /> A Moros mage and a Geist could benefit from a cemetery, mortuary or other place were death is strong and very simbolic. A werewolf too, if the place attracts spirits and the gauntlet is weak and bleeds some essence resonating with the place. So a cemetary could give mana, essence and plasm 'cause its thematically acceptable. From a Zen garden, well, no plasm for Geists.<br /> <br /> It's only a house rule that I try to apply with common sense. It is also a good theme for conflicts/alliances with other supernatural splats.<br /> <br /> But returning to the books, nope, I think that the rule is one place = one soda flavor. If I am wrong, I will appreciate that someone here correct me <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> About Changelling I don't recall if they have something similar to a place of power. They have their dimension pockets and get their glamour from goblin fruits or harvesting it from emotions or dreams, but something like a mage/werewolf/geist &quot;sacred place&quot;... I think they have not such a thing, but I don't know it for sure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12340,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","user":"dourden","date":". 02-09-2017, 01:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12340-dourden","name":"dourden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T07:14:12-08:00","id":1046753,"title":"","content":"1. Unless he's using mudras (hand gestures), mantras (spoken formulae), or something undeniably occult like reading from a grimoire or performing a ritual, a mage doesn't necessarily stand out during spellcasting. Forming the proper imago in one's mind is often all it takes.<br /> <br /> 2. 'Viewed' through Mage Sight, his spellcasting will become visible as his Nimbus flares. The book has a variety of descriptions regarding the sensory description of Nimbuses (Nimbi?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4260-terpsichordean","name":"terpsichordean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4260_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T11:11:42-08:00","id":1046846,"title":"","content":"If you want a place that gives multiple forms of 'soda' it's not really that hard to do, at least for ley lines, hallows and a locus.<br /> \u200bHallows already have some implied relationship with ley lines, often appearing near or on one and changes in local ley lines are said to affect local hallows, so just place your hallow in close proximity to a nexus. Coincidences do happen.<br /> \u200bAs for locus, they are formed when enough resonance gathers in a location to pierce the Gauntlet. Easy explanation for ones presence is to build a story where a past Mage claimed this hallow and then proceeded to perform actions, either large 'scale' or long term, that garnered enough emotions to form a locus. Make it the site of an ancient shrine or temple, ancient religions often held caves as special places, or if a darker resonance is desired make him one of the Mad and this is where he performed his little experiments.<br /> \u200bChangelings draw their Glamour from the emotions of the living, so place it under a night club, funeral home or other site where the emotional gather.<br /> \u200bI have no idea what Death Eaters 'eat' but if ghosts are part of it any of the above uses could result in a serious haunting.<br /> \u200bAll of these sources may not be together in the literal cave but there is no reason why they couldn't exist in close enough proximity to each other to achieve the same effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T13:29:17-08:00","id":1046903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1046256-newbie-questions?p=1046846#post1046846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI have no idea what Death Eaters 'eat' but if ghosts are part of it any of the above uses could result in a serious haunting.<br /> \u200bAll of these sources may not be together in the literal cave but there is no reason why they couldn't exist in close enough proximity to each other to achieve the same effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sin Eaters gain power from 'low places' where death energy collects. Ghosts are optional but not requiered. Caves, cemeteries, basements of old houses are all pretty decent spots.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4135-blue-thomas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar4135_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4135\" data-vbnamecard=\"4135\">Blue Thomas</a> <br /> <br /> Id allow those to be in the same place as well, a Hallow that a Moros Mage used for a lot of death magic would certainly apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-10T14:01:15-08:00","id":1046920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1046256-newbie-questions?p=1046296#post1046296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Imperial Mysteries had a thinly disguised reference to the Gentry as the Old Gods of the Thistle; it's a pretty good explanation for the Gentry if they are Supernal beings. Moinen is correct though that the working assumption as of 2e is that they're different places/entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changeling Arcadia can still be a supernal emanation realm, or more likely, an astral temonic realm where the Gentry can still be the Old Gods of Thistle as well as compatible with 2e where Changeling Arcadia is definitely not Mage Arcadia.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}